defmodule EmakolaWeb.GhanaMap do
  @moduledoc """
  Ghana's sixteen regions as SVG geometry, for the directory's region picker.

  The shapes are real. What stood here before was a hand-drawn twenty-point
  blob with pins dropped on it by eye — a Ghanaian shopper could not find
  their own region on it, which is the only job the picture has.

  Boundaries come from geoBoundaries ADM1 (gbOpen, sourced from
  OpenStreetMap, CC BY-SA 2.0), projected equirectangular with a cos(lat)
  correction and simplified with Ramer-Douglas-Peucker at 0.9px in this
  viewBox. At Ghana's latitude that projection differs from a proper conic
  by well under a percent, and it keeps the transform a pure scale. The
  attribution is required by the licence and is rendered in the map's
  footer — do not remove it.

  Region names are the canonical sixteen, identical to
  `Emakola.Suppliers.GhanaRegions.all/0` and to what `Store.region` holds,
  so a name from this module can be handed straight to the directory's
  region filter and match.
  """

  @view_box "0 0 1000 1250"

  @regions [
    %{
      name: "Greater Accra",
